# The Rebirth Law  
### How Environmental Intensity Governs Burstiness and Chemical Tempo

The Rebirth Law states:

**“As the depth of the cosmic gravity well increases, both star‑formation burstiness and chemical enrichment tempo rise in direct proportion to environmental intensity.”**

This law links three domains:

1. **Environmental Pressure**  
   - gravity‑well depth  
   - tidal index (T)  
   - filamentary infall rate  
   - local density field  

2. **Star‑Formation Behavior**  
   - smooth vs bursty SFH  
   - stochastic triggers  
   - overfueling cycles  
   - runaway tidal‑chemical pumping  

3. **Chemical Evolution (Sₓ)**  
   - slow enrichment in isolation  
   - moderate enrichment under filament feeding  
   - rapid enrichment in high‑T environments  

